  "comparison": "The Ṛgvedic accusative śámīm and Atharvan śamī́m have identical letters but place their acute on different vowels. The first is tagged ritual service in this corpus, while the second is the tree climbed by the aśvattha. The Virāṭaparvan spells the name without accent.",
  "instrumental": "Three attested instrumentals singular differ in both vowel length and the presence of y. In particular śámī at three locations is instrumental, although śamī can be a nominative in two other histories.",
